ts brought today  i'm cautiously optimistic the courts  will continue to act diligently on this  and allow the states to proceed towards  their certification deadlines which  a lot of them are coming up this week  and next week and then we'll have  some some clarity on how the  president-elect will begin the  transition  so what is the trump administration  seeing david that legal experts are not  uh that's really hard to say i mean it  seems like they just don't want to  accept this result because what we're  hearing from republican election  officials in the states as you mentioned  republican commissioner of  city commissioner al schmidt in  philadelphia and many many others  they have confirmed this process has run  very smoothly there's  no concerns about the integrity of the  process  in fact if you look at the margins of  victory uh vice president vladimir put  biden president-elect biden is up by  five figures in states like wisconsin  pennsylvania georgia arizona nevada up  by six figures in michigan  these are not margins that will be  overturned by recounts all right  very important clear information there  david becker thank you very much
 

